185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (This internship focused on applying Graph Neural Networks \(GNNs\) to resting-state fMRI data for Autism Spectrum Disorder \(ASD\) classification using the ABIDE dataset. The work began with a from-scratch implementation of a 2-layer GCN on the Cora citation network to build a foundational understanding of graph convolutions and message passing. This was followed by a literature review of six papers spanning GNN benchmarking, learnable brain-network generation \(FBNetGen\), demographic-aware GNNs \(BrainADNet\), spatiotemporal GNNs \(GLNSTGNN\), attention-based brain transformers, and signed graph convolutions for handling anticorrelated connectivity. Building on this, FBNetGen was implemented end-to- end on the ABIDE dataset to generate task-aware brain graphs instead of relying on fixed Pearson-correlation adjacency matrices. Finally, a dedicated study was conducted on the latent space learned by a GCN classifier - examining, via PCA and UMAP, whether ASD/HC groups, acquisition sites, and misclassified subjects form meaningful structure in the learned embedding space, and how this compares to raw functional-connectivity representations.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
